{"kind":"request","text":"Security R5 (6dd06d03 sections 1.5, 2.1, 2.4 and 5): hosted MCP endpoint.\n\nWork:\n1. The hosted MCP endpoint answers only when a deployment setting turns it on. Without the setting, /mcp and /mcp/agents answer 404 and create no object.\n2. The default tool mode leaves out `create`, `install_application`, `credential`, `prepare`, `join` and the raw reads `record`, `step` and `text`. A deployment setting adds them back by name.\n3. A tool hidden for lack of a grant refuses when called by name (packages/mcp/src/service.ts:353-357).\n4. A bearer has an end, 30 days by default. A `bearer` control renews it. An expired bearer answers 401.\n5. A stored control answer keeps no bearer plaintext. The first answer shows it once. A replay of the same `op` answers that the bearer was shown and does not show it again.\n6. The `#failures` record has a bound.\n7. The registry's `#expire` write runs only after the control signature passes (1.5).\n\nWitnesses: one for each item. The head's report lists, for each Worker that uses the endpoint, the tools its running agents call and the settings that keep them working.\n\nCloses 2.1, the bearer half of 2.4, and 1.5.\n\nCommon conditions (6dd06d03, review of main 603220b9). Checker review of each exact head before it lands. A head can close part of this request; each head names the findings it closes. The hosted Workers (artroom-scope, dap-grow, dap-lending) stay deployable after each head: the head's report lists every new setting and redeploy step, and the planner deploys after review. No deployment by the builder. Place in the security order: 5 of 10 (6dd06d03 assert lists the order). The archive slices keep priority when one of them is ready to work: F1, 9a, slice 9, F2 (land by 4 November) and F3 (deploy by 6 November).","body":{"conditions":"Opt-in endpoint, narrow tool default, hidden tools refused, bearer expiry, no stored bearer plaintext, bounded failures, expire after signature; closes 2.1, 2.4 bearer, 1.5. Checker review on every head; hosted Workers stay deployable; no builder deployment.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}